        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0509" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg413"/>

                <head>No. 234.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Washburne.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 10,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 616.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatches numbered 968, 969, 970, and 971.</p>
                <p>Referring to your No. 968, relating to a convention for the amelioration of the
                    condition of prisoners of war, to be held at Brussels in July next, it does not
                    seem that the United States are called upon to take part therein.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
